35,2,1,talk,May,,The complaint log shows one household filed eleven of fourteen complaints. The measurements show the narrowest frontage is only ninety centimetres. This is a trap.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The station block’s bin house smells worse than the open pile by midsummer. The truck comes at seven forty. A narrow window means waking up before dawn.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The subsidy covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand. Last year’s shelters averaged two hundred forty-eight thousand. Plus thirty-four thousand a year on nets and deodorant.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"At the residents' meeting, nobody volunteered to turn away a late bag. The station block is still fighting over a broken latch. We need a plan that keeps us talking.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The filing requires four months and five signatures. Supervised mornings average fifty minutes each. That’s a lot of hours just in paperwork and oversight.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, thirty-four thousand a year on deodorant? That’s a waste. We need a system that stops the bags from standing open, not just a bigger box.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, the smell follows the bags, not the location. But if the truck comes at seven forty, we’re waking up too early. That’s a daily annoyance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, I hear you. But if we don’t fix the cost, we can’t afford the fix. The subsidy is a lifeline, but it’s not enough for a permanent build.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, four months of paperwork is a nightmare. And if nobody wants to be the enforcer, the system fails. We need a structure that makes cooperation easy.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, exactly. The hours add up. If we rely on goodwill, it fails. We need clear, fair rules so nobody feels burdened or policed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, the truck time is fixed, but the hours we spend maintaining it are not. I need to know if this new spot actually saves us time, or just shifts the burden.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, the smell is a symptom. The real problem is nobody wants to be the enforcer. We need a system that doesn’t require us to police each other.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I agree. A system that relies on goodwill fails. We need clear, fair rules so nobody feels burdened or policed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, clear rules are good, but they don’t stop people from resenting each other. We need a structure that makes cooperation easy, not just mandatory.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, easy cooperation is the goal. But I need to know the hours. Does the new spot save us time, or just shift the burden?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
